;
; How Mockingbird files one emulated device in MYRA (mockingbird_rules.h
; MR5): its place on the map, its kind (uart, timer, display ...), the base
; and size of its region in bytes (a 48-bit address space fits 15 digits)
; and the irq it is wired to. Mockingbird asks whether the numbers fit
; before it lists them.
^ZXMOCK(device:i2) = kind:i2! ^ base:i15! ^ size:i15! ^ irq:i3!
